; oat — oberon-agent-tool — the stateless serial client for AgentTool.Mod on a
; live (booted) Oberon system, ported from the oberon-agent Rust CLI.
; Layered bottom-up: Data (the operation + wire vocabularies) — Device (the
; byte channel) — Io (wire codec + retry) — Tool_call (the typed operations) —
; Cli (parse / render / wiring); Error is the failure vocabulary they share.
; Wrapped, so the modules read Oat.Tool_call / Oat.Io / ... from outside.
; The executable lives in bin/; the on-system half lives in Mod/.

; risc_core appears only for U32 (the u32 <-> LE-byte codec shared repo-wide);
; the emulator itself stays behind the serial FIFO surface.

(library
 (name oat)
 (libraries risc_core oberon_tools unix))
